<article class="env-lemma" id="0ETE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ETE">Lemma <span data-tag="0ETE">34.10.4</span>.</a> Let $\{ T_ j \to T\} _{j = 1, \ldots , m}$ be a standard V covering. Let $T' \to T$ be a morphism of affine schemes. Then $\{ T_ j \times _ T T' \to T'\} _{j = 1, \ldots , m}$ is a standard V covering. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(V) \to T'$ be a morphism where $V$ is a valuation ring. By assumption we can find an extension of valuation rings $V \subset W$, an $i$, and a commutative diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(W) \ar[r] \ar[d] &  T_ i \ar[d] \\  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(V) \ar[r] &  T }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       By the universal property of fibre products we obtain a morphism $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(W) \to T' \times _ T T_ i$ as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>